看那,看那尘埃,看那兴奋.

326
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:08,320
This is the last group of elephants, and amongst them there, in the middle.
这是最后一群大象 中间还有它们

327
00:18:08,320 --> 00:18:11,320
That's the one I've been waiting for, that's Iraq.
那是我一直在等待的,那就是伊拉克。

328
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:15,320
Now, here's one of the ones that we moved from Nairobi just recently.
这是最近我们从内罗毕搬来的

329
00:18:15,320 --> 00:18:20,320
And he has made a relationship with Nacilok, she's like his mum.
他和纳西洛克建立了关系 她就像他的妈妈

330
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:24,320
And wherever she goes, he tries to follow, just coming through the middle here.
不管她走到哪里 他都想跟随他 只是从中间走过来

331
00:18:24,320 --> 00:18:31,320
The tiniest of all, looking just a touch confused, but knows what's good for him.
最微小的,看起来只是有点困惑, 但知道什么对他有好处。

332
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:39,320
And just going past him, I think that's Nacilok.
刚刚经过他,我想那是纳西洛克。

333
00:18:39,320 --> 00:18:41,320
That's his surrogate mother.
那是他的代理母亲

334
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:44,320
Just a touch of nervousness, and you'd expect it.
只是有点紧张,你会期待的。

335
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:50,320
This little elephant didn't come to the orphanage until he was 18 months old.
这只小象直到18个月才来到孤儿院.

336
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:53,320
So he knew all about his wild family.
故知其野家之所为.

337
00:18:53,320 --> 00:18:55,320
He knew what he was missing.
他知道他错过了什么

338
00:18:55,320 --> 00:18:58,320
When he was orphaned, his mother got sick, she died.
当他成为孤儿时,他的母亲生病了,她死了.

339
00:18:58,320 --> 00:19:03,320
And a year and a half, he was suddenly torn away from his complete support system.
而一年半,他突然从他的完整支持系统中撕裂.

340
00:19:03,320 --> 00:19:04,320
Look.
听着

341
00:19:04,320 --> 00:19:09,320
Now, you see, nervous, where's mum?
你看,紧张,妈妈呢?

342
00:19:09,320 --> 00:19:11,320
Where's my new mum?
我的新妈妈呢?

343
00:19:11,320 --> 00:19:13,320
He's looking for Nacilok.
他在找纳西洛克

344
00:19:13,320 --> 00:19:14,320
Where is she?
她现在在哪?

345
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:16,320
He's on the search, look.
他正在寻找,看。

346
00:19:16,320 --> 00:19:19,320
Look at the difference between him and the other elephants.
看看他和其他大象的区别

347
00:19:19,320 --> 00:19:22,320
All the other elephants, quiet, relaxed.
所有其他大象,安静,放松。

348
00:19:22,320 --> 00:19:23,320
And he's looking for somebody.
他在找一个人。

349
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:25,320
Here comes Nacilok.
纳西洛克来了

350
00:19:25,320 --> 00:19:29,320
See the trunk go out.
看后备箱出去。

351
00:19:33,320 --> 00:19:35,320
And that's what he needs right now.
而这正是他现在需要的。

352
00:19:35,320 --> 00:19:39,320
He needs that reassurance to keep us and not enough for him.
他需要这种保证来留住我们 而对他来说还不够.

353
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:44,320
And that's the reason why Nacilok actually joins a rock.
这就是纳西洛克真正加入岩石的原因.

354
00:19:44,320 --> 00:19:48,320
To keep him calm, to keep him settled.
为了让他冷静,让他安顿下来.

355
00:19:48,320 --> 00:19:50,320
Totally different behavior now.
现在行为完全不同了

356
00:19:50,320 --> 00:19:54,320
Once mum's that big presence behind him, just reassuring.
一旦妈妈在他身后出现,只是安慰。

357
00:19:54,320 --> 00:19:57,320
And of course that's what he'd get from his mother.
当然,这是他从他母亲那里得到的。

358
00:20:01,320 --> 00:20:06,320
One of the things that I love about elephants, and you can see it happening right here in front of you,
我最爱大象的东西之一 你可以在眼前看到

359
00:20:06,320 --> 00:20:09,320
is the empathy that they have for one another.
他们是互相怜悯的。

360
00:20:09,320 --> 00:20:11,320
These two elephants aren't related.
这两头大象不相关.

361
00:20:11,320 --> 00:20:16,320
It's not a mother and girl, but you'd never know it, because they really do seem to care.
这不是一个母亲和女孩, 但你永远不会知道, 因为他们似乎真的在乎。

362
00:20:16,320 --> 00:20:22,320
And actually, I think it's essential to a rock for little elephant to have that kind of nurturing right now.
事实上,我认为小象现在要养成那样的石头 是必不可少的。

363
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:27,320
He needs it, and Nacilok knows it, and she's prepared to give it to him.
他需要它,而纳西洛克知道,她准备把它给他.

364
00:20:27,320 --> 00:20:29,320
That's just the most wonderful thing.
这是最美妙的事情。

365
00:20:31,320 --> 00:20:34,320
So, life's looking great for a rock.
所以,生活看起来棒极了

366
00:20:34,320 --> 00:20:40,320
And the keepers tell me that the other two little lilies who came up with him have also settled in really well.
守门人告诉我,另外两只小百合 和他一起来的,也已经安顿得很好。

367
00:20:40,320 --> 00:20:41,320
But what about Wendy?
但是温蒂呢?

368
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:46,320
Well, it looks as if things have really turned around for her too.
看来事情也为她翻了头.

369
00:20:46,320 --> 00:20:49,320
I mean, just look at Wendy.
我是说 看看Wendy

370
00:20:49,320 --> 00:20:53,320
Now, when we brought those three little orphans from Nairobi up here to a thumber,
现在,当我们把三个孤儿 从内罗毕带到这里,

371
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:56,320
we thought that Wendy perhaps would adopt the role of the matriarch.
我们以为温蒂或许会接受母权

372
00:20:56,320 --> 00:20:58,320
She would be like a mother to them.
她会像一个母亲 他们。

373
00:20:58,320 --> 00:21:01,320
Well, it didn't happen, but look at her now.
嗯,它没有发生, 但看看她现在。

374
00:21:01,320 --> 00:21:07,320
She's beginning to actually move away from that dependence on people and become an elephant,
她开始摆脱对人的依赖 变成一只大象

375
00:21:07,320 --> 00:21:11,320
to be part of the herd, just to have fun, just to enjoy herself.
成为牧群的一部分, 只是为了玩乐, 只是为了享受自己。

376
00:21:11,320 --> 00:21:16,320
Nacilok says if she's growing up a little bit, but very much now connected with being an elephant,
纳西洛克说,如果她长大了一点点, 但现在很多与做大象有关,

377
00:21:16,320 --> 00:21:19,320
and that's just what we wanted.
这就是我们想要的

378
00:21:19,320 --> 00:21:22,320
So, what could have prompted Wendy's change of heart?
那么,什么能促使Wendy改变心意?

379
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:27,320
Maybe, with three new babies in the herd occupying the keepers' attention,
也许,有3个新婴儿 占据了守护者的注意力,

380
00:21:27,320 --> 00:21:32,320
she decided it was time to look to the other elephants for companionship again.
她决定是时候再次寻找其他大象的陪伴了

381
00:21:32,320 --> 00:21:40,320
We'll never know the answer, but what I can definitely say is that she's back to being her old happy self again.
我们永远不会知道答案 但我可以肯定的说 她又回到了她快乐的过去

382
00:21:40,320 --> 00:21:47,320
Up in Nairobi, it's a big day for Underlolo.
在内罗毕,今天是英特洛大日子。

383
00:21:47,320 --> 00:21:53,320
After weeks of treatment, it's time to see if there's been any improvement in his eyesight.
经过几周的治疗,是时候看看他的视力是否有改善.

384
00:21:53,320 --> 00:21:58,320
The result could decide whether he has any chance of a life back in the wild.
结果可以决定他有没有机会回到野外生活.

385
00:21:58,320 --> 00:22:03,320
Angela Scheldrick Daffney's daughter has brought the vet to see him.
安吉拉·谢尔德里克 达夫尼的女儿带兽医去看他

386
00:22:03,320 --> 00:22:11,320
Angela, there's no question the opacity is much reduced.
安吉拉,毫无疑问不透明度已经降低了

387
00:22:11,320 --> 00:22:13,320
There's no question of that.
亦无此疑.

388
00:22:13,320 --> 00:22:15,320
And he is a bit visual.
他有点视觉。

389
00:22:15,320 --> 00:22:22,320
He can see me, he could see, he could distinguish myself a little bit, and that's why he was looking at me.
他可以看到我,他可以看到, 他可以区分自己一点点, 这就是为什么他看着我。

390
00:22:23,320 --> 00:22:26,320
But also, all these other senses have compensated.
但是,所有这些其他感官都得到了补偿。

391
00:22:26,320 --> 00:22:27,320
Yeah.
对

392
00:22:27,320 --> 00:22:28,320
That's the bird eye, Sanjay.
这是鸟眼,桑杰。

393
00:22:28,320 --> 00:22:29,320
Yeah.
对

394
00:22:29,320 --> 00:22:32,320
See the wind just just on there.
看到风就在那里。

395
00:22:32,320 --> 00:22:33,320
I can see the thunder.
能见雷霆.

396
00:22:33,320 --> 00:22:35,320
I can see the thunder. I can see it.
能见雷霆. 我看得出来

397
00:22:35,320 --> 00:22:37,320
This is really good.
这是非常好的。

398
00:22:37,320 --> 00:22:39,320
I'm not surprised you can see so well.
我并不惊讶你能看得这么清楚

399
00:22:39,320 --> 00:22:41,320
So you think there's definitely some vision?
所以,你认为肯定有一些视觉?

400
00:22:41,320 --> 00:22:43,320
Yeah, definitely.
当然.

401
00:22:43,320 --> 00:22:44,320
Definitely.
当然

402
00:22:44,320 --> 00:22:46,320
Yeah.
对

403
00:22:46,320 --> 00:22:47,320
Light and dark and shape.
光阴和形.

404
00:22:47,320 --> 00:22:48,320
Yeah.
对

405
00:22:48,320 --> 00:22:49,320
Yeah.
对

406
00:22:49,320 --> 00:22:50,320
Exactly.
没错

407
00:22:52,320 --> 00:22:54,320
You're going to be all right.
你会没事的。

408
00:22:54,320 --> 00:22:56,320
Isn't that amazing?
这难道不惊人吗?

409
00:22:56,320 --> 00:23:02,320
It's fantastic news for everyone, especially under low-low.
这对每个人来说都是个好消息, 特别是在低调下。

410
00:23:02,320 --> 00:23:14,320
It's nightfall in Ithumba and the elephants have returned to the stock aid.
伊通巴之夜,大象已归股援.

411
00:23:14,320 --> 00:23:19,320
They sleep behind electric fences to keep them in and predators out.
他们睡在电栅栏后面,以阻止它们进入和捕食者进入.

412
00:23:19,320 --> 00:23:27,320
Using specialized equipment, I'm going to get a unique insight into what Wendy and Iraq do once the lights go out.
使用专用设备,我会得到一个独特的洞察 一旦灯光熄灭,温迪和伊拉克会做什么。

413
00:23:27,320 --> 00:23:31,320
It's such a privilege to come up to the stock aid at night.
晚上去买股票真是荣幸

414
00:23:31,320 --> 00:23:33,320
I mean, it's a different world.
我的意思是,这是一个不同的世界。

415
00:23:33,320 --> 00:23:38,320
Because after all, remember the night, particularly for the little ones, must be really scary.
因为毕竟,记住这个夜晚,特别是对于小的来说,一定非常可怕.

416
00:23:38,320 --> 00:23:42,320
Little Iraq recently having moved here from Nairobi.
小伊拉克最近从内罗毕搬到这里.

417
00:23:42,320 --> 00:23:48,320
I mean, if it wasn't for Nastalok, this big elephant that's acting as mum to them, this would be a really tough time for them.
我是说,如果不是纳斯塔洛克, 这头大象对他们来说是妈妈, 对他们来说,这将是一个非常艰难的时刻。

418
00:23:50,320 --> 00:23:59,320
Now, next door to Nastalok and Iraq and these elephants, we've got the youngsters, the adolescents.
现在,Nastalok和伊拉克的隔壁 还有这些大象, 我们得到了年轻人,青少年。

419
00:23:59,320 --> 00:24:01,320
We've got Wendy and her charms.
我们有温蒂和她的魅力

420
00:24:01,320 --> 00:24:04,320
And, I mean, they are just like a naughty bunch of school kids.
他们就像一群淘气的学童

421
00:24:04,320 --> 00:24:09,320
They've been sent to bed, the lights are out, and suddenly it's like, okay, is it safe?
他们被送去睡觉了,灯光熄灭了,突然间,好像,好了,安全了吗?

422
00:24:09,320 --> 00:24:10,320
Can we just start mucking around?
我们能开始乱来吗?

423
00:24:10,320 --> 00:24:12,320
I mean, they're having such fun.
他们玩得很开心

424
00:24:16,320 --> 00:24:25,320
You can see that Iraq is determined to stay as close as he can, just as he does during the daytime, to Nastalok, to his surrogate mum.
你可以看到,伊拉克决心尽可能地与他保持密切联系,就像他在白天所做的那样,与纳斯塔洛克、他的代孕母亲保持密切联系。

425
00:24:25,320 --> 00:24:32,320
And, I mean, it must be so comforting for him because, remember, this little elephant, he lost his herd.
我是说,他一定很舒服 因为,记住,这头小象,他失去了他的牲畜

426
00:24:32,320 --> 00:24:38,320
He lost his mum when he was 18 months old, so he has a real memory of the wild herd.
他18个月大的时候就失去了母亲,因此对野兽群有着真正的记忆.

427
00:24:38,320 --> 00:24:42,320
So this must be just heaven for that little elephant.
所以,这一定是天堂 对于小象。

428
00:24:44,320 --> 00:24:48,320
Next door, Wendy's thoroughly enjoying her newfound friendships.
隔壁 温蒂很享受她新发现的友谊

429
00:24:48,320 --> 00:24:52,320
She's not allowing her sleepover charms to get any rest at all.
她不会让她的宿醉魅力 得到任何休息。

430
00:24:52,320 --> 00:24:57,320
You can see Nastalok's eyes now just beginning to droop.
你可以看到纳斯塔洛克的眼睛 现在刚刚开始运行。

431
00:24:57,320 --> 00:25:02,320
She's obviously very tired, and the reason I'm sure it is, is because she's got new responsibilities.
她显然非常疲惫,而我敢肯定,原因就是她有新的责任.

432
00:25:02,320 --> 00:25:08,320
She's got a little elephant, little or rock to look after, and it's obviously taking it out of her.
她有一头小大象,小的或石头要照顾,显然它从她身上取出.

433
00:25:09,320 --> 00:25:15,320
There she goes. Nastalok's finally given in. She's just toppling over, just going down on her side.
她来了 Nastalok终于屈服了 她只是翻过来, 只是下去在她身边。

434
00:25:15,320 --> 00:25:19,320
Oh, that must feel so good.
哦,这一定很舒服。

435
00:25:19,320 --> 00:25:29,320
You can see that Iraq, I mean, it's just like during the daytime.
你可以看到伊拉克, 我的意思是, 它就像白天。

436
00:25:29,320 --> 00:25:36,320
He wants to be as close as he possibly can to Nastalok, so he's curled up there, and he's right just between her legs.
他想尽可能接近纳斯塔洛克 所以他在上面卷曲着 就在她两腿之间

437
00:25:36,320 --> 00:25:40,320
It's just like a cradle for him. He must feel so contented doing that.
这就像一个摇篮给他。 他一定觉得很满意

438
00:25:40,320 --> 00:25:49,320
That's lovely. The way Wendy and the others now, they finally had enough.
真可爱 温蒂和其他人现在 终于受够了

439
00:25:49,320 --> 00:25:52,320
The party's over, and they're going to get some sleep.
派对结束了,他们要睡觉了

440
00:25:52,320 --> 00:25:59,320
This really proves to me that both Wendy and Iran have found their place in the family.
这真的证明 温迪和伊朗都在家庭中找到了他们的位置

441
00:25:59,320 --> 00:26:01,320
They seem so content.
他们看起来很满意

442
00:26:07,320 --> 00:26:16,320
Up in Nairobi, morning brings unexpected and totally devastating news.
在内罗毕,早晨带来出乎意料的、完全毁灭性的消息。

443
00:26:16,320 --> 00:26:25,320
Little Andalolo has died very suddenly, and the keepers are in shock.
小安达洛洛突然去世,守门人大惊小怪.

444
00:26:36,320 --> 00:26:55,320
He was fine. I started coming back, putting on weight, lively, feeding well.
他没事 我开始回来,放重物,活泼,喂得好好的。

445
00:26:55,320 --> 00:27:01,320
And then he just suddenly went off his food in the morning and was dead an hour later.
然后他突然离开 他的食物在上午 一小时后死亡。

446
00:27:02,320 --> 00:27:06,320
So, we were all devastated, of course.
所以,我们当然都受到了打击。

447
00:27:06,320 --> 00:27:13,320
Tragedy was that we really thought he had a chance, and he did say one to live.
悲剧是,我们真的认为 他有机会, 他确实说一个人活着。

448
00:27:13,320 --> 00:27:21,320
We all loved him to bits, but it was not to be.
我们都爱他一点,但它不是.

449
00:27:21,320 --> 00:27:29,320
Edwin has seen his share of tragedies here, but this death has hit him very hard.
埃德温在这里看到了他那份悲剧,但这次的死亡使他深受打击.

450
00:27:30,320 --> 00:27:33,320
I feel very sad and very shocked about it.
我对此感到非常悲伤和震惊。

451
00:27:33,320 --> 00:27:36,320
Of course, I loved that baby elephant.
当然 我爱那头小象

452
00:27:36,320 --> 00:27:47,320
The trusted absolutely everything they could to save this little calf.
相信他们能拯救的小犊子的一切

453
00:27:47,320 --> 00:27:52,320
Across their three centres, they currently care for over 50 orphaned elephants,
在他们的三个中心, 他们目前照顾50多头孤儿大象,

454
00:27:52,320 --> 00:27:56,320
but almost the same number have been rescued and not made it.
但几乎相同数目的人被救出来,但没有成功。

455
00:27:56,320 --> 00:27:59,320
And these are tough statistics for the team to live with.
这些是团队难以忍受的数据。

456
00:27:59,320 --> 00:28:05,320
Every elephant is precious, but for Daphne and the whole team in Nairobi,
每只大象都很珍贵 但对于达芙妮和内罗毕的团队来说

457
00:28:05,320 --> 00:28:08,320
this particular little elephant will never be forgotten.
这只小象永远不会被遗忘

458
00:28:08,320 --> 00:28:14,320
And the fight to save Kenya's wild orphans will go on.
拯救肯尼亚野生孤儿的斗争将继续下去。

459
00:28:14,320 --> 00:28:22,320
Next time on Elephant Diaries, we've just heard from Daphne that another orphan has been brought into the stockade up a boy,
下一次在大象日记上 我们刚从Daphne那里听说 另一个孤儿被带进储藏室

460
00:28:22,320 --> 00:28:26,320
and I'm just hoping that it's in a lot better condition than it will and Delolo was.
我只是希望它的状况 比它会好很多 和德洛洛。

461
00:28:26,320 --> 00:28:28,320
Let's go and check him out.
我们去看看他

462
00:28:28,320 --> 00:28:37,320
To discover more about elephants and the people who work with them,
为了更多了解大象和与之合作的人

463
00:28:37,320 --> 00:28:41,320
visit bbc.co.uk/nature.
请访问bbc.co.uk/nature。

464
00:28:41,320 --> 00:28:46,320
And if you miss super giant animals with Steve Bakshor,
如果你想念超级巨型动物和史蒂夫・巴克肖尔,

465
